\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Single-factor evaluation of the Maxwell--Kronecker projection over the full campaign range. Panels as in Fig.~\ref {main-fig:compression} of the main paper. In~(c) the retained energy fraction approaches the white-noise floor $r/I=1/16$ at $-20$~dB while the \emph  {uncompressed} spectral gap $\sigma _{K+1}/\sigma _K$ reaches $0.99$ and the compressed one $0.81$: this is the diagnostic form of delay-pole collapse, and the gap between the two curves is the margin the projection buys.}}{8}{}\protected@file@percent }
